From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 19:14:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hnetcfg: firewall profile settings, the older profile
 objects, INetFwMgr questions

The settings of INetFwPolicy2 per profile (block all inbound, notifications, unicast responses,
default inbound/outbound action, excluded interfaces) are kept in the profile keys under
SharedAccess\Parameters\FirewallPolicy where Windows keeps them, and read back; writing needs
an administrator (the registry refuses anyone else). RestoreLocalFirewallDefaults clears them
and the stored rules and has Stained Glass Firewall reset through sg-admind. INetFwPolicy::
GetProfileByType and INetFwProfile (Type, FirewallEnabled through the firewall's status and
sg-admind, exceptions not allowed, notifications, unicast responses) share those settings.
INetFwMgr gets CurrentProfileType, RestoreDefaults, IsPortAllowed (from the enabled inbound
allow rules of the profile in use; restricted when a rule has a remote scope) and
IsIcmpTypeAllowed (from the ICMP settings values).

